# Walk artifacts (2026-08-20). These are outputs of a measurement run, not source: screenshots taken
# while diffing a page against its mockup, and *.partial.json written by a prover that was interrupted
# mid-sweep. `git add -A` before a release would otherwise commit them. The FINISHED reports that gates
# read (e.g. failure_injection_report.json) are deliberately NOT matched by these patterns.
*.partial.json
dayplanner_after_*.png
hive-after-*.png
index-anon-*.png
index-ops-home-*.png
index-viewport-*.png

# Narrowed spot-check artifacts (2026-08-27). A --page / --journey / --persona / --surface run now
# writes its OWN report so it cannot clobber the full sweep's verdicts - see
# tools/validate_report_clobber_guard.py. Those copies are throwaway diagnostics for attributing one
# gap; the banked truth is always the un-suffixed file, which stays tracked.
*_results.*.json
*_report.*.json
.bank_depth_receipt.json

# VD wave: real vehicle documents downloaded for extraction fixtures (binaries stay local;
# manifest.json + *.truth.json ARE committed - provenance + hand-read truth)
_fixtures/vehicle_docs/*.pdf
_fixtures/vehicle_docs/*.docx
_fixtures/vehicle_docs/*.xlsx
_fixtures/vehicle_docs/*.xls
# W4 wave (2026-09-14): real internet-sourced upload fixtures for the seven upload pages. The FILE stays local
# (a real CMMS export, an OEM manual, a nameplate photo, a part photo, listing photos, a technician resume, a
# short audio clip); manifest.json - the provenance (source URL, licence, sha256, fetched date) - is tracked.
_fixtures/cmms-export/*
_fixtures/fault-photo/*
_fixtures/part-photo/*
_fixtures/listing-photo/*
_fixtures/technician-resume/*
_fixtures/audio-clip/*
!_fixtures/*/manifest.json

